+# Spec: Order filtering on "My Orders"
+
+## Goals
+
+- Let a customer narrow the "My Orders" list down to the order(s) they're
+  looking for, without scrolling a long unfiltered list.
+- Support filtering by order status (e.g. processing, shipped, delivered,
+  cancelled) and by a date range the order was placed in.
+- Filters must be combinable (status AND date range at once).
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Full-text search over order contents (item names, SKUs) — a separate,
+  larger feature; out of scope here.
+- Filtering/sorting by dollar amount — not requested and not addressed.
+- Any change to the admin-side order management tooling.
+
+## Requirements
+
+1. The "My Orders" page exposes a status filter (multi-select) and a
+   date-range picker (start date, end date).
+2. Selecting a status and/or date range re-queries and re-renders the
+   order list to show only matching orders; an empty result shows an
+   explicit "no orders match these filters" state, not a blank list.
+3. Filters persist across pagination — see "Interaction with pagination
+   and sorting" below.
+4. Clearing all filters returns to the original unfiltered, default-sorted
+   list.
+
+## Interaction with pagination and sorting
+
+The source issue doesn't mention this, but it must be decided: filtering
+changes the *result set*, not the page size or sort order. When a filter
+is applied, pagination resets to page 1 of the filtered set (page numbers
+are relative to the filtered result, not the original list), and the
+existing sort order (most-recent-first) is preserved and applied to the
+filtered set rather than being reset.
